  "notes": [
    "Only candidate_restriction variants enter the primary ranking against SPATHI.",
    "ARACNe3 is TF-restricted but undirected, so it enters topology analyses rather than the directed confirmatory family.",
    "pySCENIC-GRN delegates network inference to GRNBoost2; it is executed and reported only against GRNBoost2 as an implementation sensitivity and does not enter the primary Friedman ranking.",
    "External competitors use exact locked ToolSpec defaults without benchmark tuning. Only caller seeds and non-parameter input/execution contracts may differ.",
    "Methods that cannot consume tf_list form a separately labelled all-gene-inference exploratory stratum; evaluation remains on the simulator-declared TF-to-gene truth universe.",
    "SCING is blocked because its upstream defaults are dimensionally invalid for part of the declared v1 panel; v1 does not retune methods to make them fit.",
    "scMINER is blocked because its default species-specific driver resources do not overlap synthetic identifiers; changing driver_source would be competitor tuning.",
    "scGeneRAI and scSGL are excluded because their locked implementations contain uncontrolled stochastic operations and expose no seed parameter.",
    "scMTNI indep=true,q=0 passes group_native preflight but rejects multigroup datasets at runtime; group_emulated is not a supported ToolSpec mode.",
    "ANDREA preflight is authoritative for dataset-specific eligibility."
  ]
